<script>
  import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.pulse';
</script>

<Navbar />

<main class="docs-page">
  <aside class="sidebar">
    <h3>Components</h3>
    <nav>
      <a href="/docs/components" class="active">Overview</a>
      <a href="/docs/components#creating">Creating</a>
      <a href="/docs/components#props">Props</a>
      <a href="/docs/components#composition">Composition</a>
      <a href="/docs/components#braces">Literal Braces</a>
    </nav>
    <a href="/docs" class="back">← All Docs</a>
  </aside>
  
  <article class="content">
    <h1>Components</h1>
    <p class="lead">Build reusable UI components with Pulse's component system. Each component is a self-contained unit with its own logic, template, and styles.</p>

    <section id="creating">
      <h2>Creating Components</h2>
      <p>Components are <code>.pulse</code> files in the <code>components/</code> directory.</p>
      
      <div class="file-tree">
        <div class="file-header">📁 Project Structure</div>
        <div class="file-content">
          <div class="file-item folder">src/</div>
          <div class="file-item folder indent">components/</div>
          <div class="file-item file indent-2">Button.pulse</div>
          <div class="file-item file indent-2">Card.pulse</div>
          <div class="file-item file indent-2">Navbar.pulse</div>
          <div class="file-item folder indent">pages/</div>
          <div class="file-item file indent-2">index.pulse</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">components/Button.pulse</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  // Component logic
  const { label, variant = 'primary', onClick } = props;
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;button 
  class={`btn btn-${variant}`}
  onClick={onClick}
&gt;
  {label}
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  .btn {
    padding: 10px 20px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  
  .btn-primary {
    background: #6b46c1;
    color: white;
  }
  
  .btn-secondary {
    background: #e5e7eb;
    color: #374151;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="props">
      <h2>Component Props</h2>
      <p>Props are passed as attributes and available via the <code>props</code> object.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">Passing Props</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  import Button from './components/Button.pulse';
  import Card from './components/Card.pulse';
  
  function handleClick() {
    alert('Button clicked!');
  }
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;!-- String props --&gt;
&lt;Button label="Click Me" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Expression props --&gt;
&lt;Button label={dynamicLabel} onClick={handleClick} /&gt;

&lt;!-- Multiple props --&gt;
&lt;Card 
  title="Welcome"
  description="This is a card component"
  image="/hero.jpg"
/&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Default Props</h3>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code is:raw>// Using destructuring with defaults
const { 
  label = 'Button',
  variant = 'primary',
  size = 'medium',
  disabled = false
} = props;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <h4>💡 Props Best Practices</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Use destructuring for cleaner code</li>
          <li>Provide sensible defaults</li>
          <li>Keep props minimal and focused</li>
          <li>Document expected prop types in comments</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="composition">
      <h2>Component Composition</h2>
      <p>Compose complex UIs by nesting components.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="label">components/Card.pulse</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  import Button from './Button.pulse';
  
  const { title, description, actions } = props;
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;div class="card"&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;{title}&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;{description}&lt;/p&gt;
  
  &lt;div class="card-actions"&gt;
    &lt;Button label="Learn More" variant="secondary" /&gt;
    &lt;Button label="Get Started" variant="primary" /&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
  .card {
    background: white;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  }
  
  .card-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Page Using Components</h3>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;script&gt;
  import Navbar from './components/Navbar.pulse';
  import Card from './components/Card.pulse';
  import Button from './components/Button.pulse';
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;Navbar /&gt;

&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Welcome&lt;/h1&gt;
  
  &lt;div class="grid"&gt;
    &lt;Card 
      title="Feature One" 
      description="Amazing feature description"
    /&gt;
    &lt;Card 
      title="Feature Two" 
      description="Another great feature"
    /&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  
  &lt;Button label="Get Started" onClick={goToSignup} /&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="braces">
      <h2>Expressions &amp; Literal Braces</h2>
      <p>
        <code is:raw>{expression}</code> is evaluated everywhere in the template, including inside
        <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;code&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>.
        Only <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> bodies are raw.
      </p>
      <p>
        To show code samples with literal braces, add <code>is:raw</code> to the element: its children are
        emitted verbatim (no expressions, no components) and the attribute is removed from the output.
        For a single literal brace, use <code>&amp;#123;</code> and <code>&amp;#125;</code>.
      </p>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code is:raw>&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;{snippet}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;          &lt;!-- renders the value of snippet --&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code is:raw&gt;{snippet}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;   &lt;!-- renders the text {snippet} --&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="reference">
      <h2>Quick Reference</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Pattern</th>
            <th>Example</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Import</td>
            <td><code>import Button from './Button.pulse'</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Access Props</td>
            <td><code is:raw>const { label } = props;</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pass String</td>
            <td><code>&lt;Button label="Click" /&gt;</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pass Expression</td>
            <td><code is:raw>&lt;Button onClick={fn} /&gt;</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Self-Closing</td>
            <td><code>&lt;Navbar /&gt;</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

